# What this file is for: @mpd-dsh/silicon is distributed as a clone, so the wrong
# ignore here ships a broken bundle (a missing dist row cannot load) or leaks local
# state. The "must be committed" list below is deliberate, not an oversight.

# ── MUST BE COMMITTED (do not add ignore rules for these) ───────────────────
#   packages/*/dist/index.js   the bundle patch loads dist/index.js directly; a
#                              clone without it installs rows that cannot resolve
#   skills/**                  the RTL corpus, served by the bootstrap row
#   packages/mpd-bundle/cordis.patch.yml   the bundle patch itself
#   scripts/**                 build, pack and gate scripts
#   docs/**                    (when present) user documentation

# ── Ignored ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.venv*/
# MP (the plugin's own local state): team state, memory journals, boulder state.
.mpd/

# Local code-intelligence index (tool state, not project content).
.codegraph/

# Packer staging output. NOTE the trailing slash and the leading slash: the pattern
# must match the top-level dist/ DIRECTORY only, never packages/*/dist (which is
# committed) — an unanchored `dist/` would silently drop every plugin artifact.
/dist/

# Local scratch / temporary working directories.
.tmp-*
.tmp/
*.tmp

# Local toolchain and QA sandboxes (mirrors the source project's layout, where
# these are throwaway install targets rather than shipped content).
.toolchain/
.qa-*/
.qa-tmp/

# Editor / OS noise.
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.idea/
.vscode/

# Node package-manager state that is reproducible from package.json.
.npm-cache/
.pnpm-store/
*.log
